  "steps": [
    "Marinade: blend the red onion, garlic, adobo sauce, ancho powder, 1 tbsp olive oil, cumin, oregano, water, salt, and pepper until smooth. Toss with the chicken in a zip-top bag and refrigerate at least 30 minutes or overnight.",
    "Roast the poblano: set it directly over a gas flame or under the broiler, turning, until blackened all over, 8 to 10 minutes. Seal in a covered bowl for 10 minutes, then peel, seed, and finely chop half of it for the corn salsa.",
    "Rice: bring the 4 cups water to a boil, add the rice, a pinch of salt, and the bay leaf, and boil until tender, 10 to 12 minutes. Drain, rinse with hot water in a fine-mesh sieve, discard the bay leaf, and stir in the cilantro, lime juice, and lemon juice. Season with salt.",
    "Corn salsa: cook the corn according to the package directions and spread it on a sheet pan to cool. Toss with the red onion, chopped poblano, jalapeño, cilantro, and lemon and lime juice. Season with salt.",
    "Tomato salsa: combine the tomatoes, red onion, cilantro, jalapeños, and lemon and lime juice. Season with salt.",
    "Guacamole: scoop the avocados into a bowl, add the lemon and lime juice, and mash. Fold in the red onion, jalapeño, cilantro, and salt.",
    "Heat the remaining 1 tbsp oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Sear the chicken on both sides until it reaches 165°F inside, 5 to 7 minutes per side. Rest 5 minutes, then chop into bite-size pieces.",
    "Assemble the bowls: rice, chicken, black beans, both salsas, guacamole, and cheese."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Use the other half of the roasted poblano in eggs or quesadillas."
  ],
